1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,400
The old bloodstains collected
from Bai Wen's home

2
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,590
were retested,

3
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:14,820
(Part One: Basic Case Information)
and found to be type A.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,440
Liang Chao's medical examination
records from the hospital

5
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,550
also show type A blood.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,870
The bloodstains show a spatter pattern

7
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:22,480
consistent with blunt force impact.

8
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:23,510
This proves

9
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:25,510
that Liang Chao was attacked

10
00:00:25,510 --> 00:00:26,550
in Bai Wen's warehouse.

11
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:29,600
Captain Qin, the test results are back.

12
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:30,870
Chief Zhao.

13
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:33,350
The tissue paper found at the scene

14
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:35,070
was Linglong Supermarket's own brand.

15
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,920
It perfectly matches

16
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,790
the fibers found in Liang Chao's
airway that caused his death by asphyxia.

17
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:42,840
Huo Qicheng was one of the organizers

18
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,070
of the Longfan Urban
Construction Fundraising Case.

19
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:46,070
Liang Chao was his deputy,

20
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:50,200
and his wife, Jin Juan,
handled the actual operations.

21
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:51,790
Our investigation shows

22
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:54,750
that Jin Juan had helped Huo Qicheng

23
00:00:54,750 --> 00:00:56,710
handle the flow of the raised funds.

24
00:00:56,920 --> 00:01:00,430
All three were at the center
of the fundraising case.

25
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:01,750
Judging by the method used,

26
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,240
all three victims

27
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:05,150
suffered hammer blows to the head.

28
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:07,510
So I believe blows
to the head with a hammer

29
00:01:07,590 --> 00:01:09,590
are a method this killer commonly uses.

30
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,150
Chief.

31
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:13,840
Chief Zhao.

32
00:01:24,230 --> 00:01:26,200
This serial murder case

33
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:27,350
is extremely serious.

34
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:29,790
We have a clear picture of the case now.

35
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:31,350
Qin.

36
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:32,950
Investigate the cases together.

37
00:01:33,230 --> 00:01:34,020
Yes.

38
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:37,940
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 10=

39
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,020
(Injection Room)
Doctor Lin.

40
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,680
Mrs. Zhou is behind
on her hospital fees again.

41
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,280
She's already received
two payment notices.

42
00:01:42,510 --> 00:01:43,590
Her son came this morning

43
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:45,040
and sat crying in the hallway.

44
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,400
He said they
really can't afford it anymore.

45
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,040
But she still needs treatment.

46
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,070
I know about her family's situation.

47
00:01:51,350 --> 00:01:53,280
Her family was also cheated in
that urban construction

48
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:54,200
fundraising case, right?

49
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,680
Doctor Lin.

50
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,640
We really can't afford
to keep her in the hospital.

51
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:01,560
We can't pay the fees.

52
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:04,480
Go take care of your work first.

53
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,280
Doctor Lin.

54
00:02:10,590 --> 00:02:12,680
My husband and I lost our entire

55
00:02:13,150 --> 00:02:14,560
life savings.

56
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,750
Now the property
is sitting there unfinished,

57
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,120
and our money is gone too.

58
00:02:20,190 --> 00:02:22,590
Getting sick has only made things worse.

59
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:24,360
Can I just stop treatment?

60
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:26,240
Mrs. Zhou.

61
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,310
You need treatment.

62
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:30,710
And you still have to go
on with your life.

63
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:32,190
As for the money,

64
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,870
I'll talk to the hospital and see

65
00:02:33,870 --> 00:02:35,150
if they can let you owe it for now.

66
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:37,080
You can pay it back slowly
when you have the money.

67
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:39,080
If that doesn't work,

68
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:42,710
I'll pay it for you first.

69
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:43,560
No.

70
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:44,430
Doctor Lin.

71
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:47,150
I... I can't let you pay
for my treatment.

72
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,710
I couldn't do that.

73
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,960
Just focus on getting better.

74
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,150
Don't worry about anything else.

75
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,120
Tell me,

76
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:56,430
how can people be so different?

77
00:02:57,030 --> 00:02:58,240
That Huo Qicheng

78
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,240
and his lackey Liang Chao

79
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,680
were horrible.

80
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:03,000
Mr. Liang.

81
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,120
That money we invested

82
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:06,400
was everything my husband
and I had saved our whole lives.

83
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:07,870
He has a heart condition

84
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:09,360
and was so upset
that he ended up in the hospital.

85
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,030
Please have mercy on us.

86
00:03:13,910 --> 00:03:15,240
It's all written in the contract.

87
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,680
No refunds before the term ends.

88
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,910
Can't you read?

89
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:26,680
Mr. Liang.

90
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,590
I'll kneel before you.

91
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:31,080
Please have mercy on us.

92
00:03:32,470 --> 00:03:33,280
Madam.

93
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,560
Being poor isn't your fault.

94
00:03:37,030 --> 00:03:37,960
But being greedy

95
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:40,680
is.

96
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:43,430
Mr. Liang.

97
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:44,840
Mr. Liang.

98
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:49,280
Please have mercy on us.

99
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:50,870
I'm begging you.

100
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:52,150
Do you know

101
00:03:52,150 --> 00:03:53,840
what's most pathetic
about people like you?

102
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,400
You've been poor your whole life,

103
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:58,680
and you still think you can
get your money back by kneeling?

104
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:00,000
Dream on.

105
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,080
Mr...

106
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,030
Mr. Liang.

107
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:05,680
Please. I'm begging you.

108
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:06,910
If you want to cry,

109
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:10,120
go cry outside Mr. Huo's office.

110
00:04:11,310 --> 00:04:12,150
He's softhearted.

111
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:13,710
Mr. Liang.

112
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,270
Give us back our hard-earned money!

113
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:19,720
Give us back our hard-earned money!

114
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,190
Give us back our hard-earned money!

115
00:04:23,310 --> 00:04:27,310
You fraud! Give us back
our hard-earned money!

116
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:32,070
Back then, it was Liang Chao

117
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:33,870
who went door to door
trying to persuade us.

118
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,830
He sure knew how to talk.

119
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:38,430
I met Huo Qicheng twice too.

120
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,430
He really put on airs.

121
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:41,630
But

122
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,190
before Huo Qicheng died,

123
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,830
I saw him struggling with someone.

124
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:51,070
Who was it?

125
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:52,360
A man.

126
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:54,040
He was wearing an old hat.

127
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,390
I couldn't see his face clearly.

128
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,480
Huo Qicheng and the man

129
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,040
even started shoving each other.

130
00:04:59,430 --> 00:05:01,510
I also heard the man shouting

131
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,190
something about paying with his life.

132
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:06,630
He seemed pitiful,
but a little frightening too.

133
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:09,190
Do you remember when

134
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:10,070
and where this happened?

135
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:14,160
I don't remember the exact time.

136
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:19,120
I think it was after something went wrong
with the Urban Construction Group.

137
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:22,630
It was beside the grocery store
at the corner of Old Street.

138
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:25,120
Mrs. Zhou, are you sure?

139
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,390
I'm sure.

140
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:37,140
(Longfan City Public Security Bureau
Criminal Investigation Division)

141
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:43,310
Who's this?

142
00:05:44,870 --> 00:05:46,310
What made you think of bringing me food?

143
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,390
I'm working the night shift.

144
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:49,720
I brought it on my way.

145
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:54,310
I heard something at the hospital today.

146
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,240
I don't know if it'll help you.

147
00:05:56,430 --> 00:05:58,360
What is it? Why so mysterious?

148
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:06,430
Are you sure?

149
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:12,120
Got it.

150
00:06:15,510 --> 00:06:17,920
Hey, honey.

151
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:20,510
I've been swamped lately.

152
00:06:20,870 --> 00:06:22,270
I haven't had much time
for you and our son.

153
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,040
I'm sorry.

154
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,190
No need to apologize to me.

155
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,070
What are you doing?

156
00:06:28,070 --> 00:06:29,310
There are so many people here.
We're at work.

157
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:31,600
It's been ages since I've held you.

158
00:06:31,950 --> 00:06:33,160
We can talk about that
when we get home tonight.

159
00:06:35,070 --> 00:06:36,430
I'll go work my night shift then.

160
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:37,190
Okay.

161
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:40,000
When you're done, come home early.

162
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,270
Spend more time with our son.

163
00:06:41,430 --> 00:06:43,160
We're both out from morning
till night every day.

164
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,430
The kid's practically on his own.

165
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:45,510
Got it.

166
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,950
Our son being left on his own
isn't the main concern.

167
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,870
I'm more worried about you.

168
00:06:49,950 --> 00:06:50,950
I'm warning you.

169
00:06:51,390 --> 00:06:53,390
Keep a little distance
from Director Huang at your hospital.

170
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:55,040
I've noticed the way
he looks at you isn't right.

171
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:59,160
I added vinegar to your dumplings today.

172
00:06:59,270 --> 00:07:00,070
Eat them while they're hot.

173
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:02,070
I'm leaving.

174
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,040
Okay.

175
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,120
Bye.

176
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:05,870
Bye.

177
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:09,680
Captain Qin.

178
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,870
Come on. Let's go eat at the cafeteria.

179
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:13,680
It's lunchtime.

180
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,750
Your sister-in-law just left.

181
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,800
She brought me dumplings.

182
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:18,560
Dumplings?

183
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,270
Wait, what filling?

184
00:07:22,390 --> 00:07:23,270
What kind of dumplings?

185
00:07:23,270 --> 00:07:24,430
The kind you don't like.

186
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,720
Before Huo Qicheng died,

187
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,430
he had an argument
with a man wearing an old hat.

188
00:07:32,630 --> 00:07:33,720
The man

189
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:36,560
kept shouting that Huo Qicheng
had to pay with his life.

190
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:38,240
I don't think you mentioned this man

191
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,630
during the earlier interviews.

192
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:40,360
Right.

193
00:07:40,430 --> 00:07:42,920
The witness also described the man.

194
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,310
She couldn't see his face clearly,

195
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,430
but his behavior and tone

196
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:48,240
were quite frightening.

197
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:51,920
It was as if when he said
Huo Qicheng had to pay with his life,

198
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:53,800
he was determined to make it happen.

199
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,310
If that's true,

200
00:07:56,190 --> 00:07:57,950
then he may have been gradually

201
00:07:57,950 --> 00:07:59,120
driven to anger by Huo Qicheng

202
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,630
and pushed to the brink
by the fundraising case

203
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,160
before he began taking revenge.

204
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,480
So what you're saying is,

205
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,160
this person

206
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,480
was probably the least

207
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,120
noticeable one in the crowd.

208
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,160
I keep having a bad feeling.

209
00:08:12,390 --> 00:08:13,190
What if

210
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:15,240
we stop disturbing that butterfly

211
00:08:16,390 --> 00:08:17,800
and just let everything stay as it is?

212
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,040
You take care of yourself
and get a checkup every year.

213
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,480
I'll wait for you
in 2020 so we can meet.

214
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,920
Wouldn't that be good too?

215
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:26,430
Of course I'm looking forward

216
00:08:26,430 --> 00:08:28,270
to us meeting in 2020 too.

217
00:08:28,830 --> 00:08:30,680
But do you remember something

218
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,920
I once told you?

219
00:08:32,030 --> 00:08:34,080
Once we decide to take that first step,

220
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,440
there's no turning back.

221
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,030
I just don't know

222
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:42,200
whether fate will change again

223
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,320
if we catch the killer.

224
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:47,360
Ming, remember what Dad tells you.

225
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:49,390
There's nothing to be afraid of.

226
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:51,000
I've never met

227
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,270
a criminal I couldn't catch.

228
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:53,390
Dad.

229
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:55,910
That's what you told me
when I was little.

230
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,150
But didn't you disappear
while chasing criminals?

231
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,360
How did I grow up?

232
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,720
How did Mom get through
these past thirty years?

233
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:02,840
You'll never know.

234
00:09:04,390 --> 00:09:06,510
Son, what's wrong?

235
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,240
Haven't you and Mom been doing well?

236
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:18,120
Ming.

237
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:20,200
Ming.

238
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:23,000
Dad, were you calling me?

239
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,270
Move aside.

240
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:26,440
Okay.

241
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:14,740
(Winter 2000)

242
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:34,910
I'm telling you, stop calling me.

243
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:37,320
I'm not coming to see you again.

244
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:47,150
Hello, 110?

245
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:48,790
Please come save my parents.

246
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,270
Someone broke into my house.

247
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,600
Please come save them.

248
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,200
Right now,

249
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,870
(Longfan Urban Construction)
I do need your help.

250
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,440
These four people

251
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,910
all had ties to
the Longfan Urban Construction Group

252
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:10,960
(Longfan Urban Construction)
in 1990.

253
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,750
And the autopsies showed

254
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:14,510
that all four cases
involved hammer blows.

255
00:11:14,670 --> 00:11:17,360
Could we also combine
the Riverside Skeleton Case

256
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:19,870
and treat all four
as a serial murder case?

257
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,270
We can't rule out that possibility.

258
00:11:22,790 --> 00:11:23,550
Lin Tao, Qin Ming.

259
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:24,320
We have a case.

260
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,080
Let's head to the scene.

261
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:26,200
Go.

262
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:36,500
(Crime Scene Investigation. Police)

263
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:48,320
The caller is Li Yan, twenty years old.

264
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:49,270
He's repeating
his senior year of high school.

265
00:11:49,550 --> 00:11:51,440
By the time we arrived,
the killer had already fled.

266
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,630
Li Yan's parents died
despite emergency treatment.

267
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:54,960
The victims, Li Tingxiang and Ding Hua,

268
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,390
were high school teachers
at No. 2 High School in the city.

269
00:11:56,390 --> 00:11:58,630
We're checking everyone

270
00:11:58,630 --> 00:11:59,510
who entered or left today.

271
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:00,910
So far, we haven't found anything.

272
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:02,150
Captain, we're done.

273
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,510
At the time of the crime,
he locked himself in his room.

274
00:12:05,670 --> 00:12:06,320
When we arrived,

275
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,790
he opened the door and came out himself.

276
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,030
He was in a dazed state at the time.

277
00:12:09,030 --> 00:12:10,510
He's been taken
to the hospital for treatment.

278
00:12:10,510 --> 00:12:11,510
When we arrived,

279
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:12,790
both bodies were lying face down.

280
00:12:12,790 --> 00:12:13,790
The paramedics turned them over

281
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:14,960
while trying to save them.

282
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:15,960
There was so much blood.

283
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,550
A resident downstairs
also called the police.

284
00:12:17,550 --> 00:12:18,790
What time did Li Yan call the police?

285
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,670
5:40.

286
00:12:19,670 --> 00:12:21,360
He said the killer
was attacking them when he called.

287
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,910
The ambulance arrived at 6:00.

288
00:12:22,910 --> 00:12:24,320
They were pronounced dead
after resuscitation failed.

289
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,790
That was at 6:30.

290
00:12:25,790 --> 00:12:27,480
So when the ambulance arrived,

291
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,720
the victims still had vital signs.

292
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:29,670
Right.

293
00:12:31,510 --> 00:12:32,670
Based on the time of the call,

294
00:12:32,670 --> 00:12:34,200
the attack was still happening at 5:40.

295
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,720
The victims weren't dead yet,

296
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,200
but the killer
had already left the scene.

297
00:12:53,630 --> 00:12:55,270
The victims cried for help
and lost a lot of blood.

298
00:12:55,390 --> 00:12:56,670
A passerby also called the police.

299
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,480
Other than normal signs of daily life,

300
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,390
nothing in the house had been disturbed.

301
00:13:08,390 --> 00:13:09,910
It doesn't look like
a burglary turned murder.

302
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:10,870
No threats.

303
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:12,320
(Police, Public Security)
The killer attacked and left right after.

304
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:13,840
It was a targeted attack.

305
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,870
The door lock is intact.

306
00:13:15,870 --> 00:13:17,360
There are no signs of forced entry.

307
00:13:18,390 --> 00:13:19,200
Could it be

308
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,360
that they opened the door themselves?

309
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:22,840
Could the killer be someone they knew?

310
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:28,080
There's still fresh meat
and vegetables in the fridge.

311
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,360
They were probably about to make dinner.

312
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:36,300
(Model Student, Li Yan)

313
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:39,900
(Third Prize, Longfan City
Mathematical Olympiad)

314
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,320
This schedule is planned
down to the minute.

315
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:56,390
Other than bathroom and meal breaks,

316
00:13:56,790 --> 00:13:58,550
he studies from 5:30 a.m.

317
00:13:58,550 --> 00:13:59,750
to 12:00 midnight.

318
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:01,630
He only gets 15 minutes
of rest each day.

319
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,790
He even has to
practice English listening.

320
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:10,200
These are all his study materials
for repeating his senior year.

321
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:13,320
Looks like the whole family
put everything into supporting him.

322
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:15,080
They were determined to get him
into Tsinghua or Peking University.

323
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,440
Let's prepare for the autopsies.

324
00:14:18,510 --> 00:14:19,320
Okay.

325
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:26,860
(Tsinghua Campus)

326
00:14:35,550 --> 00:14:36,320
It fell.

327
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,000
Ming.

328
00:14:37,390 --> 00:14:39,480
Mom has to work the night shift
at the hospital tonight.

329
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,870
Dad will be home later.

330
00:14:40,870 --> 00:14:42,510
Be good and stay home by yourself.

331
00:14:42,510 --> 00:14:43,670
Lock the door from the inside.

332
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:45,840
Don't open it for anyone except Dad.

333
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:46,600
Understand?

334
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:47,960
Yes, Mom.

335
00:14:49,790 --> 00:14:51,150
I've left the food warm in the pot.

336
00:14:51,150 --> 00:14:52,670
If you get hungry, go ahead and eat.

337
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,270
That's my good boy.

338
00:14:57,390 --> 00:14:58,550
Mom's leaving now.

339
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,720
Make sure you lock the door
from the inside.

340
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:12,150
Okay.

341
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:21,910
What's wrong?

342
00:16:24,390 --> 00:16:25,870
Nothing. Keep going.

343
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:58,260
(Winter 2000)

344
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:07,240
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

345
00:17:10,310 --> 00:17:15,090
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

346
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:23,180
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

347
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:29,040
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

348
00:17:31,070 --> 00:17:39,030
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

349
00:17:39,660 --> 00:17:44,710
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

350
00:17:46,750 --> 00:17:55,060
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

351
00:17:55,060 --> 00:18:00,910
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

352
00:18:02,370 --> 00:18:10,490
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

353
00:18:11,180 --> 00:18:16,220
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

354
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:26,040
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

355
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:33,590
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

356
00:18:33,790 --> 00:18:38,200
♪Can you hear me?♪

357
00:18:38,210 --> 00:18:42,000
♪Can you hear me?♪

358
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:49,460
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

359
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:57,200
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

360
00:18:57,530 --> 00:19:03,140
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

361
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:08,620
♪After all these years♪

362
00:19:11,130 --> 00:19:18,610
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

363
00:19:19,510 --> 00:19:20,810
♪And tell you♪

364
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:25,300
♪I haven't let you down♪
